I think we might want to wait for the official release before merging though!

As discussed in #2973 , the caching used for CSS files, JS files etc. means that whenever we change one of these file-types and then "push to production", it can be up to 20 minutes or so before things "sync up again", and during this time people might be seeing "incorrect" content.
This can be fixed by adding a `?ver=1646652613` to the end of the file's URL (with a unique number each time), but as this is a manual process we'll probably forget to do this most of the time :wink:  However we could instead automate this by making the `ver` value e.g. the md5sum of the file's content.

@mudge If/when we do this, what file-types would we need to do this for? Is MD5 a suitable algorithm for this, or do you have another recommendation? (obviously this is only a content-has-changed checksum, not a cryptographically-secure verification! :joy: )

